<BaseLayout title="Inqling: A Collaborative Card Game in Education | Will Chai" description="Inqling is a collaborative classroom card game co-created at McMaster University. Explore the card types, play format and William Chai’s role." path="/inqling-a-collaborative-card-game-in-education/"><div class="pageShell"><SiteHeader current="projects" /><main id="main" class="pageMain"><article class="archiveRecord"><p>Project archive · William Chai</p><h1>Inqling: A Collaborative Card Game in Education</h1><section><h2>A classroom card game</h2><p>Inqling was created collaboratively by students and faculty at McMaster University, including William Chai and Dr. Michael Wong. Its purpose is to encourage conversation, reflection and a sense of belonging in learning environments.</p></section><section><h2>How it works</h2><p>The original deck contains 60 cards across three types: Long Prompts, Short Prompts and Wild Cards. Players take turns drawing a card and responding. Long Prompts invite extended reflection, Short Prompts support brief exchanges, and Wild Cards introduce images, quotations or activities with room for individual interpretation.</p></section><section><h2>Creating the game</h2><p>The team developed and tested the game through a process of shared design. The original article drew on a workshop presentation written collaboratively by students in Inquiry C14. William contributed as a member of this group.</p></section><section><h2>Using Inqling</h2><p>The game was designed for student groups and classrooms. Conversations following play give participants time to reflect on the experience. Contact William for information about the project.</p></section><p><a href="mailto:me@willchai.com">Contact William Chai</a> · <a href="/projects/">Current projects</a> · <a href="/resume/">Résumé</a></p></article></main><SiteFooter /></div></BaseLayout>
